# DexKit blog content (EN, PT, ES)

When the user asks for a **blog post**, **article**, or **guide** on dexkit.com:

## Always ship three locales

Create **all three files** in the same task (unless the user explicitly asks for one language only):

| Locale | Folder | URL |
|--------|--------|-----|
| English | `content/blog/` | `https://dexkit.com/blog/{filename-without-md}` |
| Portuguese | `content/blog-pt/` | `https://dexkit.com/pt/blog/{filename-without-md}` |
| Spanish | `content/blog-es/` | `https://dexkit.com/es/blog/{filename-without-md}` |

- **Same filename** in all three folders (e.g. `deploy-token-allowance-drop-with-dexappbuilder.md`).
- **Same `slug`** in frontmatter (match filename).
- **Translate** title, excerpt, and body; keep product names (`DexAppBuilder`, `DropAllowanceERC20`, UI labels) as in the product.
- **Localized internal links** — do not link EN posts from PT/ES:

```markdown
<!-- EN -->
[DexAppBuilder guide](https://dexkit.com/blog/creating-on-chain-application-made-easy-with-dexappbuilder)

<!-- PT -->
[guia DexAppBuilder](https://dexkit.com/pt/blog/criacao-de-aplicativo-on-chain-facilitada-com-dexappbuilder)

<!-- ES -->
[guía DexAppBuilder](https://dexkit.com/es/blog/creacion-de-aplicaciones-en-cadena-simple-con-dexappbuilder)
```

Use **filename** (not frontmatter slug) in URLs when they differ across legacy posts — grep `content/blog-pt/` for the PT/ES slug of a related post.

## Frontmatter (all locales)

```yaml
---
title: 'Primary keyword + DexAppBuilder | benefit'  # EN; translate for PT/ES
date: 'May 18, 2026'   # PT: 18 de maio de 2026 | ES: 18 de mayo de 2026
excerpt: >-
  1–2 sentences, 140–160 chars: main keyword, what reader gets, DexKit/DexAppBuilder, no Solidity/no-code if relevant.
category: Blog
slug: kebab-case-matching-filename
imageUrl: /blog-images/{same-image}.png
---
```

Banner image: follow `.cursor/rules/dexkit-blog-images.mdc` and set the **same** `imageUrl` in EN, PT, ES.

## SEO structure (every post)

1. **Quick answer** — First paragraph starts with **Quick answer:** / **Resposta rápida:** / **Respuesta rápida:** One dense paragraph: what it is, main tool, 3–4 steps, primary links. Written for featured snippets and AI summaries.
2. **Hook** — 1–2 short human paragraphs (problem → why this guide).
3. **H2 as questions** where it fits: `What is…`, `…vs… which one`, `How to…`, `FAQ`.
4. **Definition block** — Plain-language “X is…” with contract/product names.
5. **Comparison table** (markdown tables supported via `remark-gfm`) when comparing options.
6. **Who is this for** — bullet list of use cases.
7. **Steps** — `##` + `###` with actionable instructions; keep UI strings in English (`Settings → Networks`, `DexGenerator`).
8. **Checklist** — copy/paste launch list.
9. **FAQ** — 5–7 questions as `###` headings; direct answers in 1–3 sentences (AI overviews).
10. **More from DexKit** — 3–5 internal links (locale-correct) + docs.dexkit.com.
11. **Get started** — 2 CTA links + contact/Discord.

**Title:** Lead with primary keyword; include `DexAppBuilder` or `DexKit` when relevant (~50–65 chars).

**Keywords:** Use naturally in H2s and first 100 words: product name, chain names, `ERC-20`, `no code` / `sem código` / `sin código`, task intent (`presale`, `claim`, `deploy`).

## AI SEO

- One **quotable definition** per core concept.
- **Entity clarity:** DexKit, DexAppBuilder, DexContracts, contract types (`DropAllowanceERC20`).
- **Tables and lists** for facts machines can extract.
- Each section answers **one search intent** only.
- FAQ questions phrased how users/search/AI ask them.

## Voice (sound human, not AI)

- Write like a teammate explaining to a builder — direct, specific, occasional “we’ve seen…”.
- Vary sentence length; mix short paragraphs with bullets.
- **Avoid:** delve, leverage, seamless, robust, comprehensive, “whether you’re a beginner or expert”, stacked em dashes, emoji CTAs, excessive `---` dividers.
- **Do:** concrete scenarios (treasury wallet, testnet before mainnet), honest troubleshooting.

## Markdown technical notes

- Inline code: `` `DropAllowanceERC20` `` → renders as `<code>` (Tailwind typography backticks are disabled in `globals.css`).
- Tables need a header row and `|---|---|` separator.
- Link docs: `https://docs.dexkit.com/...` (same for all locales).

